      "purpose": "`identifier` provides strict, immutable UUID, ULID, TypeID, KSUID, and NanoID values, compile-time domain wrappers, and explicit compatibility profiles for derived public identifiers. Each generated family keeps its own clock, entropy, ordering, leakage, and persistence contract; an identifier is never treated as a secret, authorization fact, idempotency proof, or tracing context merely because it is unique.",
